.TH PSMatrixDup 3 2024-03-09 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSMatrixDup\fR \- Duplicate matrix

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSMatrixDup\fR(\fIPSMatrix matrix\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Duplicate \fImatrix\fR by creating a new matrix having the same shape as \fImatrix\fR and by copying all values of \fImatrix\fR to the new matrix.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The new matrix or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImatrix\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] it's not possible to allocate the matrix in memory.
.RE
.RE

.br
\fBWARN\fR:  the address pointed by the returned pointer should never be freed directly. The specific function \fIPSMatrixFree\fR should be used instead.
.br

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
